supplement('M05.01','Moduli multiply under complex multiplication, so multiplying by i changes direction but leaves every distance from the origin unchanged.','复数乘法使模相乘，因此乘i只改变方向，保持到原点的距离。');
supplement('M06.03','Starting exactly at an equilibrium yields a constant sequence even when the equilibrium is unstable.','即使平衡不稳定，从平衡点精确出发仍得到常数列。');
lessons.find(l=>l.moduleId==='M25.06').prerequisites.push('module.M24.02');
lessons.find(l=>l.moduleId==='M26.04').prerequisites.push('module.M08.02');
deepen('M13.01','An upper bound need not be attained: it only has to lie above every element of the set. The supremum adds minimality. To prove s is the supremum, establish both that x≤s for every member x and that every smaller number fails to be an upper bound. Equivalently, for every ε>0 there is a member greater than s−ε. This approximation property often lets a proof approach the bound without assuming it belongs to the set. Completeness is a property of the real number system, not merely a convenient theorem about a particular set. The positive rational numbers whose squares are less than two have no rational supremum, because their missing boundary is √2. In the reals the supremum exists. This contrast explains why rational arithmetic alone cannot support all limits used in calculus.','上界只须在所有元素上方，不必取到；上确界还最小。证明s上确界需证全体x≤s，并证任何更小数不是上界，等价于任ε>0有元素大于s−ε。此性质可逼近界而不假设界属于集合。完备性是实数系统的性质；正有理数中平方小于二的集合没有有理上确界，缺失边界√2，但实数中存在，说明仅有理运算不能支撑全部微积分极限。','For the set {1−1/n : n is a positive integer}, what is the supremum?','集合{1−1/n：n为正整数}的上确界多少？',1,'Every term is below 1, but choosing n large makes it arbitrarily close to 1.','各项小于1，n足够大时任意接近1。','One is an upper bound. Given ε>0, choose n>1/ε so 1−1/n>1−ε; therefore no smaller upper bound works.','1是上界；任ε取n>1/ε，则1−1/n>1−ε，故更小数不能作上界。');
deepen('M13.02','The convergence definition requires one tail of the sequence to satisfy the error bound for every later index. For a_n=2+3/n, requiring |a_n−2|<ε reduces to n>3/ε, explicitly constructing a valid threshold. A subsequence selects increasing indices; every subsequence of a convergent sequence has the same limit, so two subsequences with different limits disprove convergence. Cauchy sequences compare late terms to each other without naming a proposed limit. In a complete metric space every Cauchy sequence converges, but this need not hold in the rationals. On the real line an open set contains a small interval around each of its points. A closed set contains limits of its convergent sequences, connecting topological language to the numerical limit definition. Boundedness alone is insufficient for convergence, as the alternating sequence shows.','收敛定义要求同一尾部让所有更晚项满足误差。a_n=2+3/n时误差<ε化为n>3/ε，明确构造阈值。子列取递增下标，收敛列的所有子列同极限，所以两个不同子列极限可否定收敛。柯西只比较晚项彼此，不先指定极限；完备空间柯西必收敛，有理数不保证。实线开集在每点含小区间，闭集包含内部收敛列的极限。有界不够，如交错列。','What is the smallest positive integer n with |(2+3/n)−2|<0.1?','满足|(2+3/n)−2|<0.1的最小正整数n多少？',31,'Solve the strict inequality 3/n<0.1.','解严格不等式3/n<0.1。','The condition is n>30, so the smallest integer is 31; n=30 gives equality and is excluded.','要求n>30，最小31；30只取等而不满足。');
deepen('M13.03','Compactness provides finite control over an infinite set. The open-cover definition says that if open neighborhoods together cover every point, finitely many already suffice. For a continuous function on a compact domain, the image is compact; in the real line it is closed and bounded, so the supremum and infimum belong to the image and are attained as extrema. Uniform continuity is stronger than pointwise continuity because one input tolerance must work everywhere, rather than depending on the chosen point. A continuous function on a compact domain is uniformly continuous. Without compactness, familiar conclusions can fail: f(x)=1/x on (0,1) is continuous but unbounded, and f(x)=x on (0,1) has neither a maximum nor a minimum. These examples show which hypothesis prevents escape toward a missing boundary.','紧致把无限集变成有限控制：开邻域覆盖全部点时有限个已足够。紧域连续像紧，在实线闭且有界，所以确界属于像并取到。一致连续要求一个输入容差全域通用，而逐点可依点；紧域连续必一致连续。无紧致可失败：1/x在(0,1)连续却无界，x在(0,1)无最大最小，显示紧致阻止向缺失边界逃逸。','A continuous function f(x)=1/x is restricted to [2,5]. What is its maximum?','连续函数1/x限制在[2,5]，最大值多少？',0.5,'The function decreases for positive x, and both endpoints are included.','正x时函数递减，端点均包含。','The maximum occurs at x=2 and equals 1/2. Compactness guarantees attainment; monotonicity locates it.','最大在x=2取1/2，紧致保取到，单调定位置。');
deepen('M13.04','For a bounded function, a lower Darboux sum uses the infimum on each partition interval and an upper sum uses the supremum. Refining a partition can only raise the lower sum and lower the upper sum. Riemann integrability is equivalent to making their difference arbitrarily small. For a continuous function on a compact interval, uniform continuity controls the oscillation on every sufficiently short subinterval, proving this property. A function equal to one on rationals and zero on irrationals has lower sums zero and upper sums equal to the full interval length, so it is not Riemann integrable despite being bounded. Differentiation is a separate local limit operation. The fundamental theorem connects them under stated assumptions; it does not erase the need to establish continuity or another sufficient hypothesis for the version being applied.','有界函数达布下和用各段下确界，上和用上确界；加细分割只能提高下和、降低上和。可积等价于差可任意小。紧区间连续的一致连续性控制每个足够短段振幅，故可积。有理点一、无理点零的函数下和零、上和为全长，虽有界却不可积。求导是另一局部极限；基本定理在适当假设下联系二者，不免除检查所用版本条件。','On [0,2], a function is 1 at rational points and 0 at irrational points. What is its upper Darboux sum for any partition?','[0,2]上有理点1、无理点0，任意分割的达布上和多少？',2,'Every nontrivial subinterval contains rational points, so each local supremum is 1.','每个非零小区间都有有理点，局部上确界一。','Each interval contributes its full width; widths sum to 2. Lower sums are zero, so the gap never vanishes.','每段贡献全宽，总宽2；下和零，差无法趋零。');
deepen('M13.05','Pointwise convergence permits the required index to depend on the point x. Uniform convergence forbids that dependence: given ε, one index must control every x in the domain. A convenient test is whether the supremum of |f_n−f| tends to zero. In x^n on [0,1], points increasingly close to one retain values near one, so no common tail makes the error uniformly small even though every fixed x<1 eventually decays. By contrast, x/n converges uniformly to zero on [0,1] because its absolute value is at most 1/n. Uniform convergence preserves continuity and, on a bounded interval for integrable functions, permits integration of the limit. Differentiating a limit requires additional control on derivatives; uniform convergence of functions alone does not supply it. Always name the operation being interchanged and the corresponding theorem.','逐点允许所需下标依赖x，一致禁止这种依赖；可检查误差上确界趋零。x^n在[0,1]中越来越靠近1的点仍接近1，尽管固定x<1会衰减，所以无统一尾部。x/n则全域≤1/n，故一致趋零。一致收敛保持连续，并在有限区间可积条件下允许极限与积分交换；求导交换还要导数控制，函数一致本身不够。必须说清交换什么操作及相应定理。','For f_n(x)=x/n on [0,3], what is sup|f_6(x)|?','f_n(x)=x/n在[0,3]，sup|f_6(x)|多少？',0.5,'The largest x is 3 and n is fixed at 6.','最大x为3，n固定6。','The supremum is 3/6=1/2. Generally the uniform error is 3/n, tending to zero.','上确界3/6=1/2；一般误差3/n趋零。');
deepen('M13.06','A metric generalizes distance while retaining the properties needed for limits: distinct points have positive distance, symmetry holds, and detours cannot be shorter than the direct distance. Open balls then generate a topology. Completeness and compactness are separate properties; a complete space may still be unbounded and noncompact. Measure adds another structure, assigning sizes to a sigma-algebra closed under complements and countable unions. Countable additivity applies to pairwise disjoint measurable sets; for overlapping sets, intersections must be accounted for. A singleton has zero Lebesgue length, yet an interval has positive length, because countable additivity does not permit treating an uncountable union as a countable sum. Integration with respect to a measure extends accumulation beyond Riemann sums and requires measurability as well as appropriate finiteness conditions.','度量保留极限所需距离性质：异点正距、对称、三角不等式，开球生成拓扑。完备与紧致不同，完备可无界非紧。测度另加结构，在对补与可数并封闭的σ代数上赋大小；可数可加要求两两不交，交叠需扣交集。单点勒贝格长度零，区间却正，因为不可数并不能当可数和。测度积分推广黎曼累积，须可测及适当有限性条件。','Intervals [0,3] and [2,5] overlap. What is the Lebesgue length of their union?','区间[0,3]与[2,5]重叠，其并的勒贝格长度多少？',5,'Subtract the overlap length from the sum of lengths.','两长度和减重叠长度。','Lengths are 3 and 3, overlap [2,3] has length 1, so union length is 3+3−1=5.','长度3、3，交长1，并长5。');
deepen('M14.01','A group is specified by both its set and its operation. The same set may support a group under one operation and fail under another: nonzero rational numbers form a group under multiplication, while all rationals include zero, which has no multiplicative inverse. Associativity concerns placement of parentheses, whereas commutativity concerns order, so they must be tested separately. An identity acts neutrally on both sides, and an inverse undoes an element on both sides. These axioms imply cancellation: multiply an equality ab=ac on the left by a⁻¹ to conclude b=c. Symmetries form groups under composition because performing one symmetry after another remains a symmetry, the unchanged configuration is the identity, and every symmetry can be reversed. Reflections and rotations can fail to commute, providing concrete nonabelian examples.','群由集合和运算共同指定。同集合在一种运算可成群，另一种未必，如非零有理数乘法成群，全体有理数因零无乘法逆而不成。结合管括号，交换管顺序，须分别查。单位元左右中立，逆元左右撤销。公理推出消去：ab=ac左乘a⁻¹得b=c。对称按复合成群，因为复合仍对称、恒等中立且可逆。反射旋转可不交换，给非交换实例。','In the multiplicative group of nonzero rational numbers, what is the inverse of 4/7?','非零有理数乘法群中4/7的逆多少？',7/4,'The inverse multiplied by 4/7 must equal multiplicative identity 1.','逆乘4/7须得乘法单位元1。','The inverse is 7/4 because (4/7)(7/4)=1. It differs from the additive inverse −4/7.','逆为7/4，乘得1，不同于加法逆−4/7。');
deepen('M14.02','A subgroup uses the same operation and identity as its parent group. For a nonempty subset, a convenient test is closure under ab⁻¹; this simultaneously ensures identity, inverses, and products. A left coset gH consists of all gh with h in H. Multiplication by g is a bijection from H to that coset, so every coset has the same size. Two cosets either coincide or are disjoint, because any shared element lets one representative be rewritten through the other. Thus cosets partition a finite group into equal blocks, proving Lagrange’s theorem. The order of an element equals the size of its cyclic subgroup, so it divides the finite group order. These consequences constrain possible structures but do not say every numerical divisor must occur as a subgroup size.','子群使用母群同运算与单位元。非空子集可用对ab⁻¹封闭检验，同时得单位、逆与乘积。左陪集gH由gh组成，乘g是H到陪集双射，所以等大。两个陪集一旦共享元素便可互写代表，因此相同或不交；有限群遂分等大块，得拉格朗日。元素阶是循环子群大小，因此整除群阶，但非每个数值因数都必对应子群。','A finite group has 42 elements and a subgroup has 7. How many left cosets are there?','有限群42元素，子群7元素，左陪集几个？',6,'Cosets partition the group into equally sized blocks of seven.','陪集分成每块七元素。','The index is 42/7=6.','指数42/7=6。');
deepen('M14.03','A homomorphism f satisfies f(ab)=f(a)f(b), so it also sends identity to identity and inverses to inverses. Its kernel contains exactly the elements sent to identity. If k is in the kernel, then f(gkg⁻¹)=f(g)f(k)f(g)⁻¹ is identity too, proving normality. This is the property that makes multiplication of cosets well-defined: changing representatives must not change the resulting coset. The quotient collapses all elements differing by a kernel element, and the first isomorphism theorem identifies this quotient with the image. To use the theorem concretely, compute the kernel and image separately, then describe the induced bijection. For finite groups, the size relation follows: group order equals kernel size times image size.','同态保乘积，故也保单位和逆。核是映到单位元的元素；k在核时f(gkg⁻¹)仍单位，证明正规。正规使陪集乘法与代表无关。商把相差核元素者合并，第一同构定理把商识别为像。使用时须分别求核像，再说明诱导双射；有限群有群大小等于核大小乘像大小。','A homomorphism from a 24-element group has image size 6. What is its kernel size?','24元素群的同态像大小6，核大小多少？',4,'Use the finite kernel-image size relation.','用有限核像大小关系。','|ker f|=24/6=4.','核大小24/6=4。');
deepen('M14.04','An action lets group elements move objects while respecting identity and composition. The orbit of an object collects all positions reachable by the action; its stabilizer consists of group elements that leave it fixed. Map a group element g to the object gx. Elements reach the same image precisely when they lie in the same coset of the stabilizer, which proves the orbit-stabilizer formula. Burnside’s lemma counts orbits by double counting pairs (g,x) with gx=x. Counting first over group elements gives the sum of fixed-point counts; counting over objects and using orbit-stabilizer shows each orbit contributes exactly the group size. Dividing yields the average fixed-point formula. This reasoning explains why the average is an integer despite individual group elements fixing very different numbers of objects.','作用让群元移动对象并保持单位复合。轨道收集可达位置，稳定子收集固定该对象的群元。g映gx，相同像恰对应稳定子同陪集，得轨道稳定子公式。伯恩赛德双数(g,x)且gx=x：先按g得不动点总和，先按x结合轨道稳定子得每轨道贡献群大小，除后得平均公式，也解释平均何以整数。','A group of order 20 acts on an object whose stabilizer has order 4. What is the orbit size?','20阶群作用于一个稳定子4阶的对象，轨道大小多少？',5,'Divide group size by stabilizer size.','群大小除稳定子大小。','The orbit has 20/4=5 elements.','轨道20/4=5个元素。');
deepen('M14.05','A ring combines an additive abelian group with multiplication and distributivity. Unlike in a field, a nonzero element may fail to have an inverse, and two nonzero elements may multiply to zero. An ideal is an additive subgroup that absorbs multiplication by arbitrary ring elements; in a noncommutative ring a two-sided ideal is required for a quotient ring. The absorption condition ensures that replacing representatives by congruent elements does not change the product class. In integers, every ideal is nZ, so quotienting gives arithmetic modulo n. A unit is an element with a multiplicative inverse, while a zero divisor annihilates some nonzero element. These concepts are different and checking them prevents illegal cancellation when moving from familiar real arithmetic to rings.','环结合加法交换群、乘法与分配律。非零元可能无逆，两个非零元也可积零。理想是吸收任意环元乘法的加法子群，非交换环取商需双边理想。吸收保证换同余代表不改积的类。整数理想均nZ，商给模n算术。单位指可逆元，零因子消去某非零元，两概念不同；检查可防把实数约分非法搬到环。','In integers modulo 8, what is the multiplicative inverse of 3, represented from 0 to 7?','模8整数环中3的乘法逆，以0到7表示多少？',3,'Find a residue whose product with 3 is 1 modulo 8.','找乘3模8余1的数。','3×3=9≡1 mod 8, so 3 is its own inverse.','3×3=9模8余1，所以自逆。');
deepen('M14.06','Polynomial division over a field works because every nonzero leading coefficient can be divided out. This makes the polynomial ring a Euclidean domain and permits a gcd algorithm analogous to integer division. If an irreducible polynomial p divides a product, it divides one factor, so the ideal generated by p yields a field quotient. To find an inverse of a nonzero polynomial class, use the extended Euclidean algorithm to write ap+bq=1, then reduce modulo p. The coefficient q represents an inverse of b. Irreducibility must be checked over the declared base field: x²+1 factors over the complex numbers but not over the real numbers. Over a finite field, testing for roots proves irreducibility for degrees two or three, but higher degrees may factor without any linear factor.','域上可除非零首系数，因此多项式除法成立并可作欧氏最大公因数算法。不可约p有素性，按(p)取商得域。求非零类b逆可用扩展欧氏写ap+bq=1，模p后q为逆。不可约必须相对基域，x²+1在复数可分，在实数不行。有限域中二三次无根可证不可约，高次却可能无一次因子仍分解。','How many elements are in F₃[x]/(x²+1), where x²+1 is irreducible over F₃?','F₃上x²+1不可约，商F₃[x]/(x²+1)有几个元素？',9,'Every remainder has degree below two, with two coefficients each chosen from three residues.','余式次数低于二，两系数各三选择。','Classes have unique form a+bx with a,b∈F₃, giving 3²=9 elements.','唯一表示a+bx，各系数三选，共9。');
deepen('M15.01','Write a finite group order as p^k m with p prime and p not dividing m. Sylow theory guarantees a subgroup of order p^k, states that all such subgroups are conjugate, and constrains their number to divide m and equal one modulo p. If that number is one, conjugation must preserve the subgroup, so it is normal. For order 21 and p=7, the number divides 3 and is one modulo 7, forcing uniqueness. For p=3, the number divides 7 and is one modulo 3, allowing one or seven; the arithmetic alone does not decide which. Use the full group structure or additional arguments to resolve remaining possibilities. A normal subgroup can then support a quotient, allowing the structure to be studied in smaller pieces rather than by listing every multiplication.','群阶写p^k m且p不整除m。西罗保证p^k阶子群，所有这样的子群共轭，其个数整除m且模p余一。个数一则共轭保持，故正规。21阶对p=7，个数整除3且模7余一，只能一；对p=3，个数可一或七，单靠数值不能定，须更多群结构。正规子群可取商，把结构拆成小块研究。','A group has order 35. How many Sylow 7-subgroups must it have?','35阶群必有几个西罗7子群？',1,'Their number divides 5 and is congruent to 1 modulo 7.','个数整除5且模7余1。','The divisors of 5 are 1 and 5; only 1 satisfies the congruence, forcing one.','5因数1、5中仅1满足同余，因此唯一。');
deepen('M15.02','Modules retain addition and scalar multiplication but let scalars come from a ring instead of a field. Without division, a nonzero scalar can kill a nonzero element, creating torsion. The module Z/6Z illustrates this: multiplying the class of two by three gives zero. A free module has a basis with unique finite linear combinations, but not every module is free. For a linear operator T on a vector space over F, define an F[x]-module by letting x act as T and a polynomial act by the corresponding polynomial in T. This translates operator questions into module questions. The minimal polynomial is the monic polynomial of least positive degree that annihilates the operator. Divisibility relations among such polynomials reveal invariant subspaces and organize canonical-form descriptions.','模把标量从域换成环，保留加法数乘，但无除法，非零标量可杀非零元，产生挠，如模6的[2]乘3零。自由模有唯一有限线性组合基，模未必自由。F向量空间上线性算子T可令x作用为T，构成F[x]模，多项式按T代入作用。最小多项式是最低次首一消去多项式，整除关系揭示不变子空间并组织标准形。','In the Z-module Z/10Z, what is the smallest positive integer k with k[4]=0?','Z模Z/10Z中，使k[4]=0的最小正整数k多少？',5,'Find the additive order of 4 modulo 10, or divide 10 by gcd(10,4).','求4模10加法阶，或10除gcd(10,4)。','The order is 10/2=5: multiples 4,8,2,6,0 first reach zero on the fifth step.','阶10/2=5，倍数4、8、2、6、0第五次到零。');
deepen('M15.03','When K contains a smaller field F, elements of K can be added and scaled by F, making K a vector space over F. Its dimension is the extension degree. If α is algebraic with minimal polynomial of degree d, polynomial division reduces every expression in α to a combination of 1,α,…,α^(d−1). Minimality proves these powers independent; otherwise a lower-degree polynomial would vanish at α. For a tower F⊆K⊆L of finite extensions, multiplying a basis of K over F by a basis of L over K produces a basis of L over F, proving the tower law. An element satisfying some polynomial may have a smaller minimal polynomial, so the degree of an arbitrary equation is only an upper bound until irreducibility is established.','K含F时是F向量空间，维数为扩张次数。α最小多项式d次时，除法把表达式降到1到α^(d−1)组合；若这些相关就有更低次消去多项式，违最小性。有限扩张塔把两层基两两相乘成总基，证明次数相乘。满足某多项式不代表该式最小，未证不可约前其次数只给上界。','A tower F⊆K⊆L has [K:F]=3 and [L:K]=4. What is [L:F]?','扩张塔[K:F]=3、[L:K]=4，[L:F]多少？',12,'Multiply dimensions using the tower law.','塔式定理使次数相乘。','[L:F]=[L:K][K:F]=4×3=12.','次数4×3=12。');
deepen('M15.04','A finite field has prime characteristic p because repeated addition of one cannot first vanish at a composite number without producing zero divisors. It is then a vector space over the prime field F_p, so finite size must be p^n. The Frobenius map x↦x^p preserves sums and products in characteristic p because intermediate binomial coefficients are divisible by p. In a finite field this injective map is also surjective, hence an automorphism. Nonzero elements form a cyclic group, allowing powers of one generator to enumerate them. A field of p^n elements is not generally the same as integers modulo p^n: the latter has zero divisors when n>1. Polynomial quotients by irreducible polynomials provide the appropriate construction. Every field element satisfies x^(p^n)=x.','有限域特征为素数p，否则一首次相加为合数零会造零因子。它为F_p上有限维向量空间，大小p^n。弗罗贝尼乌斯x↦x^p因二项系数中项被p整除而保加乘，有限集上单射亦满，故自同构。非零乘法群循环。p^n元域一般不是模p^n整数，后者n>1有零因子，应以不可约多项式商构造。每元满足x^(p^n)=x。','How many elements are in a finite field of characteristic 5 and dimension 3 over F₅?','特征5、在F₅上维数3的有限域有几个元素？',125,'Each of three basis coefficients has five choices.','三个基系数各五种选择。','There are 5³=125 elements, and 124 are nonzero.','共125元素，其中124非零。');
deepen('M15.05','A field automorphism fixing the base field must send a root of a base-field polynomial to another root of that same polynomial, because it preserves addition and multiplication. These permitted root permutations form the Galois group. For a finite Galois extension L/F, a subgroup H corresponds to the elements of L fixed by every automorphism in H. Conversely, an intermediate field K corresponds to automorphisms fixing K pointwise. The correspondence reverses inclusion: imposing more symmetries leaves fewer fixed elements. The degrees satisfy [L:L^H]=|H| and [L^H:F]=|G|/|H|. Normal subgroups correspond to intermediate extensions that are Galois over F, with quotient group describing their automorphisms. Without the finite Galois hypotheses, these equalities and the full bijection cannot be assumed.','固定基域的自同构保加乘，故把基域多项式根送到同多项式另一根，允许的根置换构成伽罗瓦群。有限伽罗瓦L/F中，子群H对应被H全部元素固定的域，反向中间域对应逐点固定它的自同构。包含反向，更多对称留下更少元素，次数[L:L^H]=|H|、[L^H:F]=|G|/|H|。正规子群对应在F上仍伽罗瓦的中间域，商群描述自同构。缺假设不可直接用。','A finite Galois extension has group order 12. A subgroup H has order 3. What is [L^H:F]?','有限伽罗瓦群阶12，H阶3，[L^H:F]多少？',4,'Use the subgroup index for the fixed-field degree over the base.','不动域在基域上次数等于子群指数。','[L^H:F]=12/3=4. The different degree [L:L^H] is 3.','[L^H:F]=4，另一个次数[L:L^H]为3。');
deepen('M15.06','A solvable group admits a chain of normal subgroups whose successive quotients are abelian; equivalently, repeatedly taking commutator subgroups eventually reaches the identity. Galois theory connects this structural property to whether polynomial roots can be expressed by field operations and radicals in characteristic zero. This does not mean every degree-five equation is unsolvable by radicals; rather, a general quintic has an unsolvable symmetric Galois group, while special quintics can have smaller solvable groups. Straightedge-compass constructions are more restrictive because each construction step introduces at most a quadratic extension. Therefore a constructible algebraic length has degree a power of two, though that condition alone does not suffice. To disprove constructibility of the real cube root of two, its irreducible cubic degree already provides the obstruction.','可解群有正规链且逐商交换，等价于反复取换位子群最终单位。特征零伽罗瓦将此联系到根能否经域运算与根式表示。不是每个五次都不可根式解，而是一般五次的对称群不可解，特殊可有较小可解群。尺规更限制，每步至多二次扩张，所以可作代数长度次数为二幂，但仅此不充分。实立方根二的不可约三次次数已阻止尺规构造。','An algebraic length has minimal-polynomial degree 6 over Q. Can it be straightedge-compass constructible? Enter 1 yes, 0 no.','代数长度在Q上最小多项式次数6，可尺规作出吗？是1否0。',0,'A constructible length must have degree a power of two.','可作长度次数必须为二的幂。','Six is not a power of two, so constructibility is impossible. This uses a necessary condition, not a claimed converse.','6非二幂，因此不可能；这里只用必要条件，未声称逆命题。');
deepen('M16.01','The Euclidean algorithm preserves common divisors because replacing a by a−qb does not change which integers divide both entries. Choose q so the remainder is nonnegative and smaller than |b|; the positive remainders strictly decrease, proving termination. The final nonzero remainder is the gcd. Recording each division also permits back substitution, expressing the gcd as an integer linear combination of the original numbers. This Bezout identity is stronger than merely knowing the gcd because its coefficients construct modular inverses and solutions of linear Diophantine equations. For positive integers, prime-factor exponents show gcd takes the smaller exponent and lcm the larger, giving gcd(a,b)lcm(a,b)=ab. Handle zero separately: gcd(a,0)=|a| when a is nonzero, while division by a zero divisor is never an algorithmic step.','欧氏算法用a−qb替a不改变共同因数。取商使余非负且小于|b|，正余数严格减，保证终止；最后非零余即gcd。记录除法可回代成原两数整数线性组合，贝祖系数能构造模逆与丢番图解。素指数中gcd取小、lcm取大，故正整数满足二者乘积ab。零须另处：非零a有gcd(a,0)=|a|，算法不能除零。','Find gcd(84,30).','求gcd(84,30)。',6,'Compute 84 mod 30, then continue with the smaller pair.','先84模30，再继续较小一对。','84=2×30+24, 30=24+6, and 24=4×6, so gcd is 6.','84余24，30除24余6，24被6整除，故6。');
deepen('M16.02','Congruence classes allow addition and multiplication because replacing an integer by a multiple-of-m difference changes the result by another multiple of m. Division is more delicate. If ax≡b mod m and g=gcd(a,m), then a solution can exist only if g divides b. When it does, divide a,b,m all by g to obtain an equivalent reduced congruence with coprime coefficient and modulus. That reduced coefficient has an inverse by Bezout’s identity. Its one solution class modulo m/g lifts to g distinct classes modulo m. This explains both the solvability condition and the number of solutions, rather than treating cancellation as ordinary fraction simplification. Always specify the range used to represent residue classes, since negative and positive representatives may describe the same class.','同余可加乘，因为换代表造成的差仍为模的倍数。除法须小心，ax≡b mod m令g=gcd(a,m)，可解需g整除b；成立时a、b、m都除g，得到系数与模互素的约化式。贝祖给逆，约化模m/g唯一类提升为模m的g个类，解释条件与解数，不能当普通分数约简。须说明余类代表范围，负正数可代表同类。','How many residue classes modulo 12 solve 8x≡4 mod 12?','模12下8x≡4有几个解类？',4,'Compute gcd(8,12) and check whether it divides 4.','算gcd(8,12)并查其整除4。','gcd is 4 and divides the right side. Reduced congruence is 2x≡1 mod 3, giving x≡2 mod 3 and four classes 2,5,8,11 modulo 12.','g=4整除4，约化2x≡1 mod3，x≡2，模12为2、5、8、11四类。');
deepen('M16.03','Unique factorization means the prime powers, not their written order, determine a positive integer. Every divisor chooses an exponent independently between zero and each exponent present in n, producing the divisor-count formula. Euler’s phi counts residues coprime to n. Removing multiples of each distinct prime factor through inclusion-exclusion yields the product formula for phi. For a prime power p^a, exactly p^(a−1) among the p^a residues are divisible by p, so phi is p^a−p^(a−1). Multiplicative arithmetic functions combine independently across coprime factors, not across arbitrary factors. For example, applying multiplicativity to 4 and 6 would be invalid because they share a prime. Keep the number of distinct prime factors separate from the total number counted with multiplicity.','唯一分解由各素数幂决定整数。约数独立选每个指数从零到现有幂，给约数数公式。φ计与n互素余类，用容斥删各互异素因子的倍数得乘积。素幂p^a中被p整除的有p^(a−1)，所以φ为差。积性函数仅对互素因子独立组合，4与6有公共素数不能直接用。互异素因子数与带重数总数须区分。','For n=72=2³·3², how many positive divisors does n have?','72=2³·3²有几个正因数？',12,'Choose the exponent of 2 from four options and of 3 from three.','2指数四选，3指数三选。','(3+1)(2+1)=4×3=12.','4×3=12。');
deepen('M16.04','Euler’s theorem can be proved by multiplying all invertible residue classes modulo m. Multiplication by a coprime a permutes those classes, so the product is unchanged; cancellation of their invertible product gives a^φ(m)≡1. Fermat’s theorem is the prime-modulus special case. For two coprime CRT moduli m,n, write x=r+mk and solve mk≡s−r mod n using the inverse of m. The result is unique modulo mn because any two solutions differ by a multiple of both coprime moduli. With noncoprime moduli, the same substitution yields a linear congruence: compatibility is r≡s modulo gcd(m,n), and the combined period is lcm(m,n). Thus the generalized method follows from the linear-congruence theorem rather than a separate unexplained rule.','欧拉可把模m所有可逆类相乘证明，乘互素a只置换集合，约去可逆积得a^φ≡1；素模即费马。两互素模CRT写x=r+mk，再模n用m逆解k，两解差同为m、n倍数，故模mn唯一。非互素时同代换成线性同余，兼容需r≡s mod gcd，周期为lcm，因此广义法直接来自线性同余。','Find the least nonnegative x satisfying x≡1 mod 4 and x≡3 mod 6.','求x≡1 mod4且x≡3 mod6的最小非负解。',9,'List values 1+4k or solve 4k≡2 mod 6.','列1+4k或解4k≡2 mod6。','k≡2 mod3 gives x=9 modulo 12. The residues agree modulo gcd 2, so the system is compatible.','k≡2 mod3，得x=9 mod12；两余数模2同，故兼容。');
deepen('M16.05','A linear Diophantine equation seeks integer points on a line. Divisibility by the gcd is necessary because every integer combination ax+by is divisible by gcd(a,b). Bezout’s identity proves sufficiency by multiplying a representation of the gcd by c/g. If (x₀,y₀) is one solution, subtracting it from another gives aΔx+bΔy=0. Dividing by g makes the coefficients coprime, forcing Δx to be a multiple of b/g and Δy the corresponding negative multiple of a/g. This derives the full parameterized family. Additional requirements such as x,y nonnegative then become inequalities restricting the integer parameter. A single valid solution proves existence, but it does not prove that every solution has been found; the subtraction argument supplies exhaustiveness.','线性丢番图求直线上整数点。gcd整除每个整数线性组合，故整除c必要；贝祖乘c/g证充分。两解相减得aΔx+bΔy=0，除g后系数互素，迫使Δx为b/g倍数、Δy为−a/g同倍数，推出全解。非负等要求再变为整数参数范围。一个解只证存在，相减论证才保证穷尽。','How many nonnegative integer solutions satisfy 2x+3y=12?','2x+3y=12有几个非负整数解？',3,'y must be even and lie between zero and four.','y须偶且在0到4。','y=0,2,4 give x=6,3,0 respectively. There are three solutions.','y=0、2、4对应x=6、3、0，共三解。');
deepen('M16.06','For a unit a modulo m, repeated powers eventually return to one because the invertible residue classes form a finite group. The smallest positive return exponent is the order, and it divides every exponent producing one. Lagrange therefore makes it divide φ(m). To find the order, factor a known multiple and test its divisors, avoiding unnecessary enumeration. For an odd prime p, nonzero squares come in pairs x and −x with the same square, and these are the only collisions, giving exactly (p−1)/2 nonzero quadratic residues. Euler’s criterion distinguishes residues through a^((p−1)/2) modulo p. These statements rely on primality; composite moduli may have more square roots of one and require factorization or other structure for analysis.','单位a的幂在有限可逆群中最终回一，最小正指数为阶，整除所有回一指数，因此整除φ(m)。求阶可分解已知倍数并试因数。奇素数p下非零平方恰x与−x成对且仅此碰撞，所以有(p−1)/2个非零二次剩余。欧拉判别以a^((p−1)/2)区分。素性关键，合数模的一可能有更多平方根，需要更多结构。','What is the multiplicative order of 3 modulo 7?','3模7的乘法阶多少？',6,'Its order divides 6; test proper divisors 1,2,3.','阶整除6，试真因数1、2、3。','3¹≡3,3²≡2,3³≡6, none is 1; 3⁶≡1, so the order is 6.','前三个相应幂余3、2、6，均非1，而六次余1，故阶6。');
deepen('M17.01','A counting argument begins by defining one outcome precisely. Selecting two books can mean an ordered pair, an unordered set, or two selections allowing repetition; those are different sample spaces. For sequential choices, multiply the number available at each stage when that count is constant for every preceding partial choice. If it varies, split into cases or sum the varying counts. For alternatives, add only after making the cases disjoint and exhaustive. To count ordered selections without replacement, the available numbers decrease one at a time. To forget order when every unordered object has exactly k! orderings, divide by k!. This division needs equal multiplicity; it is invalid when different objects are represented different numbers of times. Small explicit lists are useful for verifying what the chosen encoding counts.','计数先精确定义一个结果。选两书可能有序、无序或可重复，是不同空间。逐步选择在每种已有局面下下一步数量相同才直接乘，否则分类或求和。相加须互斥且穷尽。无放回有序选数量逐次减；若每个无序对象恰k!种顺序才能除k!，表示次数不齐不能这样除。小规模列举可核对编码究竟数什么。','A code has three positions, each chosen from four symbols, with repetition allowed. How many codes exist?','三位码每位可选四符号，允许重复，共几种？',64,'Each position retains all four choices independently of earlier positions.','每位都保留四选择。','4×4×4=64. Without repetition the count would instead be 4×3×2, a different specification.','4³=64；不许重复才是4×3×2，属于不同条件。');
deepen('M17.02','A bijection requires a well-defined map and a well-defined inverse. Describing the inverse proves both that every target object is reached and that no two source objects collapse. For example, subsets of an n-element labeled set correspond to length-n binary strings by recording membership at each position, giving 2^n subsets. Double counting does not require constructing a one-to-one map between the two descriptions; instead identify a single underlying collection counted both ways. For handshaking, the collection consists of incident vertex-edge pairs. Counting by vertices gives degree sum, while counting by edges gives twice the edge count. For a simple graph this also bounds average degree by n−1. State the incidences precisely, especially when loops or repeated edges alter conventions.','双射需良定义映射与逆；逆同时证每个目标能达且无源碰撞。n标号集合子集对应n位成员二进制串，所以2^n。双数则指定同一底层集合，不必两描述间显式配对。握手数顶点边关联，按点得度和，按边得二倍边数。简单图还给平均度≤n−1。若环重边改变约定，须精确说明关联。','A simple graph has 8 vertices, all degree 3. How many edges does it have?','简单图8点且各度3，有几条边？',12,'Count vertex-edge incidences, then divide by two.','数点边关联，再除二。','Degree sum is 8×3=24, so E=24/2=12.','度和24，边12。');
deepen('M17.03','The factorial formula for C(n,k) comes from choosing k distinct elements in order and dividing by k! possible orders for each subset. The symmetry C(n,k)=C(n,n−k) is a bijection sending a subset to its complement. Pascal’s recurrence partitions k-subsets according to whether one designated element is included. The binomial theorem counts terms in a product of n copies of (a+b): choosing b from exactly k factors yields a^(n−k)b^k in C(n,k) ways. Setting a=b=1 sums all binomial coefficients to 2^n. These identities have combinatorial meanings, so they can remain clear even before factorial manipulation. Boundary values C(n,0)=C(n,n)=1 represent the unique empty subset and full subset, not exceptional arbitrary conventions.','C(n,k)阶乘式来自有序选k个再除每子集k!排序。对称式由补集双射，帕斯卡按指定元素是否包含分类。二项式定理在n个(a+b)因子中恰k个选b，产生C(n,k)个同项。a=b=1得系数和2^n。边值C(n,0)、C(n,n)为1，分别唯一空集与全集，不是随意例外。','What is the coefficient of a³b² in (a+b)⁵?','(a+b)⁵中a³b²系数多少？',10,'Choose which two of five factors contribute b.','选五个因子中哪两个取b。','C(5,2)=5×4/2=10.','C(5,2)=10。');
deepen('M17.04','The generalized pigeonhole principle says that placing N objects into k boxes forces some box to contain at least ceiling(N/k) objects. If every box had fewer, their total capacity would fall below N. Inclusion-exclusion corrects overcounting caused by overlapping cases. For three sets, subtract pairwise intersections after adding individual sizes, then add the triple intersection back because it was subtracted too often. The alternating signs can be checked on one object belonging to exactly r sets: its net coefficient becomes one. To apply either method, define the boxes or sets explicitly; choosing them cleverly is often the central step. A result may guarantee existence without identifying an object, but it still needs a complete accounting argument rather than intuition about crowding.','广义抽屉说N物入k盒，至少一盒不少于ceil(N/k)，否则总容量不够。容斥修正交叠重复：三集先加单个，再减两两，最后加三交，因为减过头。看恰属r集的一个对象可核交替符号使最终系数一。使用前须精确定义盒或集合，巧选往往是关键。即使只保证存在不指出对象，也要完整计数。','Twenty-six objects are placed into five boxes. What minimum largest-box occupancy is guaranteed?','26物放5盒，保证最大盒至少几个？',6,'Take the ceiling of 26/5.','取26/5上整。','If every box had at most five, only 25 objects would fit. Therefore some box has at least six.','若各至多5只装25，故至少一盒6。');
deepen('M17.05','A recurrence should arise from a unique decomposition of every counted object. For balanced parentheses, match the first opening parenthesis with its partner; inside lies a smaller balanced string and afterward another, giving the Catalan convolution. The index counts pairs, not individual characters, and the empty string provides C₀=1. For set partitions, distinguish the block containing a newly added labeled element. Either it is alone, leaving a partition into k−1 blocks, or it joins one of k existing blocks. Thus S(n,k)=S(n−1,k−1)+kS(n−1,k). The k factor belongs only to the joining case. Boundary values and impossible cases must be stated to compute either recurrence without ambiguity. Counting all strings and dividing by an assumed symmetry does not substitute for this decomposition.','递推应来自每对象唯一分解。合法括号把第一个左括号与匹配右括号定位，内部与之后各是更小合法串，给卡特兰卷积，下标数对，空串C₀=1。集合划分看新标号元素所在块：独立则剩k−1块，否则加入已有k块之一，因此S(n,k)=S(n−1,k−1)+kS(n−1,k)，k只属于加入情形。须说明边界与不可能情况，不能靠不明对称随意除。','Using S(3,1)=1 and S(3,2)=3, find S(4,2).','已知S(3,1)=1、S(3,2)=3，求S(4,2)。',7,'Apply the singleton-or-join recurrence.','用单独成块或加入递推。','S(4,2)=S(3,1)+2S(3,2)=1+6=7.','1+2×3=7。');
deepen('M17.06','A generating function encodes allowed contributions to size. If an object can contribute zero, one, or two units in one way each, its factor is 1+x+x². Two independent components multiply their factors because exponent addition records total size and coefficient multiplication records paired choices. Constraints on total size become coefficient extraction rather than a separate case list. For extremal counting, separate a universal bound from a construction attaining it. For example, a simple graph on n vertices has at most one edge per unordered vertex pair, so at most C(n,2) edges; the complete graph attains this bound. If an extra restriction forbids triangles or limits degrees, the same complete-graph construction is no longer admissible, and both the bound and achieving example must be reconsidered.','生成函数编码允许大小，零一二各一种给1+x+x²。独立部件相乘，指数加记录总大小，系数乘记录配对，约束总大小转为取系数。极值须分普遍界与达到构造，如简单n点图每无序点对至多一边，故≤C(n,2)，完全图达到。加禁三角或度限制后完全图可能不合法，界和构造都须重考虑。','What is the coefficient of x³ in (1+x+x²)(1+x+x²+x³)?','(1+x+x²)(1+x+x²+x³)的x³系数多少？',3,'List allowed exponent pairs summing to three.','列允许的和为三的指数对。','Pairs are (0,3),(1,2),(2,1), each contributing one, for coefficient 3.','配对(0,3)、(1,2)、(2,1)，各一，共3。');
deepen('M18.01','A graph abstracts away physical drawing details: an edge crossing in a picture is not a vertex unless the model declares it one. A walk records successive adjacent vertices and may repeat them; a path generally avoids repeated vertices. If a walk exists between two vertices, deleting closed detours produces a path, so either notion can establish connectivity. Connected components partition the vertex set because reachability in an undirected graph is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive. In a directed graph, reachability is not symmetric; strong connectivity requires paths in both directions. Degree counts incident edge ends, while directed graphs distinguish indegree and outdegree. State whether loops contribute twice and whether repeated edges are allowed before using counting identities. The same drawn locations can therefore represent different graphs depending on these conventions.','图忽略物理画法，线交叉不自动为顶点。游走可重复点，路径通常不重复；删游走闭绕可得路径，所以两者都可证连通。无向可达具有自反对称传递，分量因此分割顶点。有向可达不对称，强连通要求双向路径。度数计关联边端，有向分入度出度；使用公式前说明环是否算两次、是否允许重边。','An undirected graph has vertices {1,2,3,4,5,6} and edges 12,23,45. How many components does it have?','无向图六点，边12、23、45，有几个连通分量？',3,'List maximal mutually reachable vertex groups, including isolated vertices.','列极大互相可达组，含孤点。','Components are {1,2,3},{4,5},{6}, so there are three.','分量{1,2,3}、{4,5}、{6}，共3。');
deepen('M18.02','Several tree characterizations illuminate different proofs. A connected acyclic graph has a unique path between any two vertices; two different paths would create a cycle. Removing any tree edge disconnects its endpoints, because an alternate connection would also form a cycle. Conversely, adding one nonexisting edge creates exactly one cycle along the prior unique path. A finite tree with at least two vertices has a leaf: take a longest path and note that an endpoint cannot have an unused neighbor without extending it. Removing a leaf preserves the tree property, so induction proves the edge count n−1. A connected graph can be reduced to a spanning tree by repeatedly deleting cycle edges without losing connectivity. These arguments explain why trees are minimal connected structures and maximal acyclic structures on their vertex sets.','树有互补刻画：连通无环使两点唯一简单路径，两路会成圈；删任一边断开，否则替代路成圈；加一新边沿旧唯一径恰成一圈。有限树至少两点时取最长路，端点不能有未用邻居，否则可延长，所以有叶。去叶仍树，归纳证n−1边。连通图反复删圈边不失连通得生成树，解释树是最小连通与极大无环结构。','A forest has 11 vertices and 3 connected components. How many edges does it have?','森林11点、3连通分量，几条边？',8,'Apply n_i−1 to each tree component and add.','每树分量用n_i−1再相加。','Total edges=Σ(n_i−1)=11−3=8.','边和11−3=8。');
deepen('M18.03','An Euler trail concerns edges: at every internal visit to a vertex, an arriving edge must pair with a departing edge. Thus all vertices have even degree for a closed Euler circuit; an open Euler trail has exactly two odd-degree endpoints. With all nonisolated vertices connected, these parity conditions are also sufficient. A constructive algorithm follows unused edges until a closed trail forms, then splices in additional closed trails wherever unused edges remain. A Hamilton cycle instead concerns visiting vertices once, so the Euler parity argument does not apply. Necessary Hamilton conditions such as connectivity are not sufficient. To avoid conflating the questions, state whether revisiting a vertex or reusing an edge is prohibited before selecting a theorem. Isolated vertices can be ignored for edge-traversal connectivity but not for a Hamilton cycle through all vertices.','欧拉关心边，内部每次到达须配离开，所以闭回路各度偶，开迹恰两个奇端点；非孤点连通时条件也充分。构造可沿未用边走闭迹，再在尚有未用边处拼接闭迹。哈密顿关心每点一次，欧拉奇偶论证不适用，连通等必要条件不充分。先说禁重复点还是边。欧拉遍边的连通可忽略孤点，遍所有点的哈密顿不可。','A connected graph has exactly two odd-degree vertices. Does it have an open Euler trail? Enter 1 yes, 0 no.','连通图恰两个奇度点，是否有开欧拉迹？是1否0。',1,'Use the parity characterization for a trail using each edge exactly once.','用每边恰一次迹的奇偶判据。','Yes: start at one odd vertex and end at the other; all other visits pair arrivals and departures.','有，从一奇点到另一奇点，其余到离可配对。');
deepen('M18.04','A matching pairs vertices through disjoint edges. In a bipartite graph with left side L and right side R, a matching saturating L assigns each left vertex a distinct neighboring right vertex. Hall’s condition is necessary because any subset S of left vertices needs at least |S| different available neighbors. Its sufficiency can be proved using augmenting paths: if a maximum matching leaves a left vertex unmatched, explore alternating unmatched and matched edges from it. If no augmenting endpoint exists, the reached vertices produce a subset with too few neighbors, contradicting Hall. This mechanism connects an existence theorem to an algorithm. Checking only the whole left side is insufficient; a small crowded subset may fail even when the total right side is large. Extra unused right vertices are allowed when only L must be saturated.','匹配以不共享端点的边配对。二分图覆盖左侧即给每左点不同邻右点，所以任左子集S至少需|S|邻居。充分性可用增广路：最大匹配仍有未匹配左点时沿非匹配与匹配边交替探索，若找不到增广末端，访问集会造邻居不足子集，反霍尔。这把存在定理连到算法。只查全左侧不够，小拥挤子集也可失败，未用右点则允许。','Left vertices A,B,C have neighbors A:{1}, B:{1}, C:{2,3}. What is the maximum matching size?','左点A邻{1}、B邻{1}、C邻{2,3}，最大匹配大小多少？',2,'A and B compete for the same single neighbor.','A、B争同一个邻点。','At most one of A,B can match; C can match separately to 2 or 3, so the maximum is two.','A、B至多一人匹配，C可另匹配2或3，最大2。');
deepen('M18.05','A coloring partitions vertices into independent sets, with no adjacent pair inside one color class. A clique of size k requires at least k colors, but this lower bound need not determine the chromatic number. A greedy algorithm using a vertex order always needs at most Δ+1 colors because at most Δ neighbor colors are forbidden at each step. Planarity concerns the existence of some crossing-free drawing, not whether one particular sketch crosses. For a simple connected plane graph with at least three vertices, each face boundary has at least three edge incidences, while each edge contributes two across faces. Combining 3F≤2E with Euler’s formula gives E≤3V−6. The bound is necessary, not sufficient, for planarity, so passing it does not prove a graph planar.','着色把点分成无内部邻边的独立集。k团至少要k色，但下界未必精确。按序贪心每点最多Δ个邻色禁用，因此≤Δ+1。平面性指存在无交叉画法，不是当前草图是否交叉。简单连通平面图V≥3时每面至少三边关联，每边跨面贡献二，3F≤2E配欧拉得E≤3V−6；此仅必要，满足不能证明平面。','A simple planar graph has 8 vertices. What upper bound on its edge count follows from 3V−6?','简单平面图8点，由3V−6得边数上界多少？',18,'Substitute V=8 into the planar edge bound.','代V=8。','3×8−6=18. Some graphs with at most 18 edges can still be nonplanar, so this is only a bound.','上界18，边数不超18仍可能非平面，所以只是界。');
deepen('M18.06','The probabilistic method proves existence by showing that a randomly chosen object has positive probability of the desired property. Indicator variables simplify counts: one indicator for each possible edge gives expected edge count by summing individual probabilities. Independence is not needed for that expectation calculation, though it matters for joint events. To rule out all bad configurations simultaneously, the union bound says their total probability is at most the sum of individual probabilities. If that sum is below one, some outcome avoids every bad event. A related argument uses a nonnegative integer count X of defects: if E[X]<1, at least one outcome has zero defects, since otherwise X≥1 always. The model must first be defined precisely, including which choices are independent and how each possible graph is weighted.','概率方法通过随机对象满足目标有正概率证存在。计数用指示变量，每可能边一个，期望由各概率相加，不需独立但联合事件需。并集界把坏事件总概率界为各概率和，和<1就有结果全避。等价地非负整数缺陷数X若期望<1必有零缺陷，否则总≥1。须先明随机模型、哪些选择独立和各图权重。','In G(5,0.3), what is the expected number of edges?','G(5,0.3)中期望边数多少？',3,'There are C(5,2) possible edges, each present with probability 0.3.','有C(5,2)条可能边，各概率0.3。','Expectation=10×0.3=3 by linearity.','期望10×0.3=3。');
deepen('M19.01','A probability model consists of possible outcomes and weights assigned consistently to events. The full sample space has probability one, the empty event zero, and disjoint event probabilities add. For a finite uniform model, event probability is favorable outcome count divided by total count, but the elementary outcomes must genuinely be equally likely. Rolling two fair dice gives thirty-six equally likely ordered pairs, not eleven equally likely sums; middle sums occur in more pairs. Complementation can simplify an event described by “at least one”: compute the probability of none and subtract from one. For overlapping events, use P(A∪B)=P(A)+P(B)−P(A∩B). Distinguish a model probability from an observed frequency in a finite experiment; frequencies fluctuate even when the model is correct.','概率模型给可能结果与一致事件权重，全集一、空集零、互斥相加。有限均匀模型以有利数除总数，但基本结果须真等可能。两公平骰是36等可能有序对，不是11等可能点数和，中间和对应更多对。“至少一个”可算“全无”补集。交叠用并概率加减交。模型概率与有限观察频率不同，正确模型下频率也波动。','Two fair dice are rolled. What is the probability that their sum is 3?','两枚公平骰子，和3概率多少？',1/18,'Count ordered pairs among the 36 equally likely pairs.','在36等可能有序对中计数。','Only (1,2) and (2,1) work, giving 2/36=1/18.','仅(1,2)、(2,1)，概率2/36=1/18。');
deepen('M19.02','Conditioning changes the reference population. Among outcomes already known to lie in B, divide the probability of A∩B by P(B) so the restricted total becomes one. Writing the same intersection as P(A|B)P(B) and P(B|A)P(A) yields Bayes’ rule. If a label can arise from several disjoint causes, the denominator is found by summing the likelihood times prior probability for each cause. This prevents ignoring base rates. For example, a rare category may remain uncommon among flagged objects even when the flag is reasonably sensitive, because many ordinary objects can also be flagged. The denominator must be positive; conditioning on a zero-probability event needs a different framework in continuous settings. A tree diagram can keep the sequence of conditional probabilities and multiplication branches explicit.','条件改变参照总体，在已知B中把交概率除P(B)归一。交概率两写法给贝叶斯。若标签可来自多个互斥原因，分母要把各原因似然乘先验相加，避免忽略基率。稀少类别即使检测灵敏，在标签对象中也可能仍少，因为大量普通对象也会被标。分母须正，连续零概率条件需另一框架；树图可明确条件顺序与分支乘法。','A box has 4 red and 6 blue balls. Two are drawn without replacement. Given the first is red, what is the probability the second is red?','盒内4红6蓝，无放回抽两次，已知首红，次红概率多少？',1/3,'After the known first draw, update both the red count and total count.','已知首抽后同时更新红数与总数。','Three red remain among nine balls, so probability is 3/9=1/3. Using 4/10 would ignore the conditioning.','剩3红共9，概率1/3，4/10忽略了条件。');
deepen('M19.03','Independence means learning one event occurred does not change the other event’s probability, when the relevant conditional probability is defined. Algebraically it is the product rule for their intersection. Pairwise independence among several events is weaker than mutual independence, which requires the product rule for every subcollection. Random variables are independent when their value events factor appropriately. An indicator variable equals one when an event happens and zero otherwise; this turns event counts into sums of numbers. For two independent fair coin flips, the head-count distribution is obtained by grouping the four equally likely ordered outcomes. Sampling without replacement usually creates dependence because the first outcome changes the composition of what remains. The model should state an independence assumption explicitly rather than treating events as independent merely because they occur at different times.','独立意为得知一事件不改另事件概率，代数为交概率乘积。多事件两两独立弱于相互独立，后者要求每个子集均乘积。随机变量独立要求值事件适当分解。指示变量事件发生取一否则零，把次数变数字和。两独立硬币的正面分布由四有序结果分组。无放回通常相关，因为首结果改剩余构成；时间不同不自动独立，模型须明说。','Independent events have probabilities 0.4 and 0.7. What is the probability both occur?','独立事件概率0.4与0.7，同时发生概率多少？',0.28,'Use the intersection product rule, justified by independence.','独立保证交概率乘法。','0.4×0.7=0.28. Without independence these two marginal probabilities would not determine the intersection.','积0.28；没有独立，仅边缘概率不能定交。');
deepen('M19.04','Expectation is a probability-weighted average, not necessarily a value the variable can actually take. A fair die has mean 3.5 even though no face shows it. Linearity follows by distributing sums over outcomes, so E[X+Y]=E[X]+E[Y] without independence. Variance measures squared deviations from the mean and is always nonnegative. Expanding the square gives the computational formula E[X²]−E[X]². Scaling X by a multiplies variance by a², while adding a constant changes its mean but not its variance. For a sum, covariance terms record dependence: Var(X+Y)=Var(X)+Var(Y)+2Cov(X,Y). Independent variables have zero covariance, but zero covariance does not generally imply independence. Keep standard deviation, the square root of variance, separate because it has the original units rather than squared units.','期望为概率加权平均，不必是可取值，如公平骰均值3.5。线性来自逐结果求和，不需独立。方差是均值平方偏离，非负，展开得E[X²]−E[X]²。数乘a使方差乘a²，加常数只改均值。和的方差还含两倍协方差，独立则协方差零，但反向不普遍成立。标准差为方差根，单位恢复原量，而方差为平方单位。','A variable X has variance 5. What is Var(3X+7)?','X方差5，Var(3X+7)多少？',45,'A shift does not change spread; scaling by 3 multiplies variance by 9.','平移不改波动，乘3使方差乘9。','Var(3X+7)=3²Var(X)=9×5=45.','方差9×5=45。');
deepen('M19.05','A binomial variable is the sum of n independent Bernoulli indicators with the same success probability p. To obtain exactly k successes, choose their k trial positions and multiply the probabilities of all successes and failures, giving C(n,k)p^k(1−p)^(n−k). Summing indicator means yields np, and independence permits adding their variances to obtain np(1−p). A geometric variable counting trials through the first success has probability (1−p)^(k−1)p for k≥1; the failures-before-success convention shifts it down by one. A Poisson variable has probabilities e^(−λ)λ^k/k!, mean and variance λ, and can approximate rare-event binomial counts under appropriate conditions. Choose a distribution by the experiment’s mechanism rather than merely by whether the observed values are integers.','二项是n个独立同p伯努利指标之和，恰k成功需选k位置，再乘成功失败概率，给C(n,k)p^k(1−p)^(n−k)。指标均值相加得np，独立使方差相加得np(1−p)。几何若数到首成功含该次，概率(1−p)^(k−1)p，若只数失败则减一。泊松概率e^(−λ)λ^k/k!，均值方差λ，适当条件下近似稀有二项。应按机制选分布，不只因取整数。','Four independent fair coin flips are made. What is the probability of exactly three heads?','四次独立公平抛币，恰三正概率多少？',0.25,'Choose the three head positions among four, then multiply the probability of one complete sequence.','选四位中三正位置，再乘一个完整序列概率。','C(4,3)(1/2)⁴=4/16=1/4.','4×1/16=1/4。');
deepen('M19.06','Markov’s inequality follows from nonnegativity: on the event X≥a, the variable contributes at least a to the expectation, so E[X]≥aP(X≥a). Applying it to the nonnegative squared deviation (X−μ)² yields Chebyshev’s inequality. These bounds need few distribution assumptions but can be conservative. For a simple symmetric random walk, increments have mean zero and variance one; independent increments give total mean zero and variance equal to the step count. Typical scale therefore grows like the square root of time rather than linearly, although individual paths can wander much farther. A concentration bound describes probability of deviations, not a guarantee that a particular path stays within a band. Stronger bounds require stronger conditions such as bounded independent increments, which must be stated rather than silently assumed.','马尔可夫来自非负：在X≥a事件上至少贡献a，所以期望≥a乘事件概率。对平方偏差应用它得切比雪夫，假设少但可能保守。简单公平随机游走每步均值零方差一，独立给总均值零、方差步数，因此典型尺度为时间平方根而非线性，单路径仍可走远。集中界描述偏离概率，不保证个体轨迹在带内；更强界需更强条件如有界独立增量，须明确说明。','A nonnegative variable has expectation 6. What Markov upper bound follows for P(X≥15)?','非负变量期望6，P(X≥15)的马尔可夫上界多少？',0.4,'Divide expectation by the positive threshold.','期望除正阈值。','P(X≥15)≤6/15=0.4. This is an upper bound, not necessarily the exact probability.','概率≤6/15=0.4，这是上界不必是精确值。');
supplement('M15.05','In the quadratic example, the subgroup containing only the identity fixes the entire extension, while the full two-element group fixes the rational base field. This explicitly demonstrates the inclusion reversal.','二次例中只含恒等的子群固定整个扩域，而完整两元群固定有理基域，直接展示包含反转。');
supplement('M16.01','The identity 6=3×18−48 proves that every common divisor of 48 and 18 divides 6; checking that 6 divides both numbers completes the gcd verification.','6=3×18−48表明每个共同因数整除6，再查6整除两数即完成最大公因数核验。');
supplement('M16.02','Modulo one there is only one residue class. Algorithms using inverse or representative conventions should treat that degenerate modulus explicitly rather than silently assuming several distinct classes exist.','模一只有一个剩余类，逆与代表约定算法应显式处理，不能默认为有多个相异类。');
supplement('M16.03','For a prime p, every residue from one through p−1 is coprime to p, giving φ(p)=p−1 directly and checking the general product formula in its simplest case.','素数p下1至p−1都与p互素，直接得φ(p)=p−1，核对乘积公式最简单情形。');
supplement('M16.04','The system x≡0 modulo 4 and x≡1 modulo 6 is impossible because the first condition makes x even while the second makes it odd. Compatibility detects this before construction.','x模4余零且模6余一不可能，前者偶、后者奇；兼容检验可在构造前发现。');
supplement('M16.05','When positivity replaces nonnegativity, parameter endpoints may be removed. For 2x+3y=12, the solutions with a zero coordinate disappear, leaving only the positive pair (3,2).','把非负改正时可能删参数端点；2x+3y=12去掉零坐标后只剩正解(3,2)。');
supplement('M17.03','The coefficient of x^k in (1+x)^n counts k chosen positions among n. A polynomial coefficient therefore has a direct subset interpretation, which later becomes the basic model for more general generating functions.','(1+x)^n的x^k系数数n位置选k，给系数直接子集解释，后续推广为一般生成函数。');
supplement('M19.04','A constant random variable has variance zero because every outcome equals its mean. Conversely, variance zero forces equality to the mean with probability one, connecting a numerical spread measure to deterministic behavior.','常随机变量各结果等均值，方差零；反向方差零迫使以概率一等于均值，把波动数值连接到确定行为。');
supplement('M19.05','A binomial count cannot exceed its fixed trial number, while a Poisson count has no finite upper support bound. This difference is essential when deciding whether an approximation could assign implausible outcomes.','二项次数不能超过固定试验数，泊松支撑却无有限上界；判断近似是否会给不可能结果时此差很重要。');
